body:
@coderabbitai Re the outside-diff finding on `.bar` (`flex-shrink: 0`): not applied, on purpose.

- `.hint` already has `flex: 0 100 auto`, so when the row is short the hint absorbs ~100× the bar's share of the shortfall. The bar loses about 1% of it, and at the 720 px window minimum it rendered untouched (checked with the real CSS in headless Chrome at 720/1180/1440 px).
- `flex-shrink: 0` on `.bar` would also apply after the hint is dismissed, which is the permanent state. A long workspace name could then no longer truncate inside the bar's ellipsis on a narrow window, and the bar would push into the "IN · …" chip. Today `.barName` truncates there, as it did before this PR.
